hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27745","Haddathana Affan who said: Haddathana Wuhayb who said: Haddathana Musa ibn Uqba from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Aqra ibn Habis that he called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind the chambers and said: O Muhammad, indeed my praise is an adornment and my blame is a disgrace; so he said: That is Allah, mighty and majestic, as Abu Salama told from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27746","Haddathana Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad who said: Haddathana Wuhayb from Musa ibn Uqba from Abu Salama from al-Aqra ibn Habis, and he said once: Indeed al-Aqra, and he mentioned the like of it."
